        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1704">

                <pb facs="1387" n="1271" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 834.00/124.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12, Paraguay.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-12-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 20, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instructions, No. 6, to
                    Mr. Turner, of August 24, 1911, I have the honor to enclose a statement showing
                    the presidential succession in Paraguay from 1870 down to the present time. As
                    will be seen, the record is marred by irregularities and violence. Since 1904
                    the country has been in a perpetual unrest, with a revolution either brewing or
                    in full blast.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nicolay A. Grevstad.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d1704-a1.xml" xpointer="d1704-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
